      "@id": "https://etriplesoft.com/odoo-implementation-process-by-etriplesoft/#faqpage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the Odoo implementation process?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The Odoo implementation process at Etriplesoft consists of 5 structured steps: Discovery &amp; Scoping, System Design &amp; Customization, Data Migration &amp; Deployment, Training &amp; User Adoption, and Go-Live &amp; Continuous Support. Each phase has defined outputs and timelines to ensure a smooth, successful ERP rollout."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does an Odoo implementation take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A typical Odoo implementation with Etriplesoft takes between 6 and 14 weeks depending on the number of modules, level of customization, and data migration requirements. Discovery takes 1–2 weeks, System Design 1–3 weeks, Implementation 2–6 weeks, Training 1–2 weeks, followed by Go-Live and ongoing support."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens during the Discovery &amp; Scoping phase?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "During Discovery &amp; Scoping, Etriplesoft consultants work with your leadership and key users to audit existing processes, identify pain points, define the module scope, and produce a Business Requirements Document (BRD) and a detailed implementation roadmap. This phase typically takes 1–2 weeks."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does Etriplesoft handle data migration during Odoo implementation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Etriplesoft follows a 4-phase data migration methodology: Extraction &amp; Mapping, Test Migration, User Validation, and Final Migration. This includes migrating master data, opening balances, historical records, and configuration data — with mandatory data cleansing to eliminate duplicates and errors before going live."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Etriplesoft provide post-go-live support after Odoo implementation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Etriplesoft provides a dedicated Hypercare period of 2–4 weeks after go-live with same-day response, daily check-ins, and rapid configuration adjustments. Long-term support tiers cover functional, technical, development, and training support under a structured SLA."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is the Odoo implementation compliant with ZATCA, ETA, and UAE FTA requirements?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Etriplesoft configures full GCC tax compliance during every Odoo implementation. In Saudi Arabia, this includes ZATCA Phase 2 (Fatoora) with cryptographic signing and clearance submission. In Egypt, it covers ETA e-invoicing with digital signatures and XML submission. In the UAE, it includes 5% VAT, FTA Form 201 returns, and Corporate Tax compliance."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What training is provided during the Odoo implementation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Etriplesoft delivers role-based training for all user groups: executives and management, department managers, day-to-day users, and system administrators. All training is conducted within the client's actual live system using real data, and includes User Acceptance Testing (UAT), documentation packages, and ongoing refresher sessions."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
