<!-- ETA HOW-TO GUIDE -->
<section class="sec eta-sec" id="eta-guide">
<div class="wrap">
 <div class="eye">ETA E-Invoicing Guide</div>
 <h2>How ETA E-Invoicing Works in Odoo for Egypt</h2>
 <p style="max-width:640px;color:rgba(255,255,255,.6)">Step-by-step: how Odoo connects to the Egyptian Tax Authority portal and handles automatic invoice compliance from day one of your implementation.</p>
 <div class="eta-steps">
 <div class="eta-step"><div class="eta-num">1</div><h3 style="">Register Odoo on ETA Portal</h3><p>Log into your ETA portal → View Taxpayer Profile → Representatives → Register ERP. Enter "Odoo" as the ERP name to receive your API credentials.</p><code>Client ID + Secret</code></div>
 <div class="eta-step"><div class="eta-num">2</div><h3 style="">Configure ETA Settings in Odoo</h3><p>Go to Accounting → Configuration → Settings → ETA E-Invoicing Settings. Enter your Client ID and Secret to connect Odoo directly to the ETA portal.</p><code>Accounting → Settings</code></div>
 <div class="eta-step"><div class="eta-num">3</div><h3 style="">Set Branch &amp; Activity Codes</h3><p>Configure a journal per company branch. Set your ETA Activity Code and ETA Branch ID. Ensure all customer contacts have correct Tax IDs and company addresses filled in.</p><code>Branch ID = 0 (single)</code></div>
 <div class="eta-step"><div class="eta-num">4</div><h3 style="">Issue Invoices — Fully Automatic</h3><p>Confirm any invoice as normal. Odoo automatically validates, digitally signs, assigns a UUID, and transmits to ETA in real time. No manual steps after initial setup.</p><code>UUID auto-generated</code></div>
 </div>
 <div style="text-align:center;margin-top:40px"><a href="https://etriple.odoo.com/appointment/3" class="btn btn-cyan">Get ETA-Configured Odoo — Free Demo →</a></div>
</div>
</section>

