 <section id="timetable">
 <h2>Class &amp; Timetable Management — Schedule Complexity, Solved</h2>
 <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;">Whether you deploy the <strong>Odoo Education Management System</strong> across one campus or multiple branches, the timetable engine applies your master-data rules and publishes schedules visible to every role instantly.</p>
 <p>A school timetable is the single most complex scheduling problem most administrators face: hundreds of classes, dozens of teachers, limited rooms, conflicting constraints. The ERP's Class &amp; Timetable module turns it into a structured master-data exercise where every class is a proper record — complete with subject, grade, teacher, room, time, and student limit.</p>
 <div class="pipeline">
 <span class="pipe-stage start">Define Subjects &amp; Grades</span>
 <span class="pipe-arrow">→</span>
 <span class="pipe-stage">Create Classes per Subject</span>
 <span class="pipe-arrow">→</span>
 <span class="pipe-stage">Assign Teachers &amp; Rooms</span>
 <span class="pipe-arrow">→</span>
 <span class="pipe-stage hold">Populate with Students</span>
 <span class="pipe-arrow">→</span>
 <span class="pipe-stage done">Publish Timetable ✓</span>
 </div>
 <div class="card-grid">
 <div class="card"><span class="card-icon">📚</span><h3>Classes with Student Limits</h3><p>Create a class for a specific subject and grade, set a maximum student capacity, and enroll only students who have opted for that subject. Over-capacity enrolment is blocked automatically.</p></div>
 <div class="card"><span class="card-icon">👨‍🏫</span><h3>Teacher &amp; Room Assignment</h3><p>Every scheduled class locks in a teacher and a physical room. Class-location master data keeps room utilisation clean and avoids double-booking.</p></div>
 <div class="card"><span class="card-icon">🗓️</span><h3>Calendar Views — Day / Week / Month</h3><p>Admins, teachers, and students see their timetable in true calendar form. Click any slot to see class details, room, and subject. The calendar syncs with exam schedules and public holidays.</p></div>
 <div class="card"><span class="card-icon">📋</span><h3>Pop-Up Class Details</h3><p>Each scheduled class opens a pop-up with date, time, location, grade, subject, teacher, and linked lesson plan — everything the admin needs to answer "where is grade 7 right now?" in one click.</p></div>
 </div>
 <p style="margin-top:1.5rem;">Students and teachers see both calendar and detailed list views of their timetable. Statuses distinguish upcoming, in-progress, and completed classes. When you need to reshuffle mid-term — a teacher goes on leave, a room becomes unavailable — you reassign on one record and every downstream view updates live.</p>
 </section>

 <section id="attendance">
 <h2>Attendance System — Daily &amp; Per-Class, Tagged &amp; Auditable</h2>
 <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;">The <strong>Odoo Education Management System</strong> supports two attendance modes simultaneously — whole-school daily and subject-level per-class — giving institutions the flexibility their operational policies require.</p>
 <p>Attendance is the most-accessed record in any school. Parents ask about it, ministries audit it, scholarships depend on it, and teachers hate marking it. The ERP makes attendance fast to capture, rich enough to explain, and permanent enough to survive any audit.</p>
 <div class="bento-grid">
 <div class="module-card"><h3>📅 Daily &amp; Per-Class Attendance</h3><ul><li>Mark overall daily attendance in one sweep</li><li>Mark per-class attendance for granular tracking</li><li>Both methods update the same student record</li><li>Multiple teachers contributing to one student's daily record</li></ul></div>
 <div class="module-card"><h3>🏷️ Tagged Absences &amp; Late Arrivals</h3><ul><li>Built-in tags: Present, Absent, Tardy, Super Tardy, Sick Leave, Excused</li><li>Add institution-specific tags with one click</li><li>Reports break down attendance by tag</li><li>Discipline workflow auto-triggers on repeated patterns</li></ul></div>
 <div class="module-card"><h3>🖥️ Optional Kiosk Integration</h3><ul><li>Entry-point kiosk for self-check-in by student card</li><li>Teacher's portal still captures classroom-level attendance</li><li>Both data streams feed one unified attendance record</li><li>Barcode / RFID card integration for speed</li></ul></div>
 <div class="module-card"><h3>🗓️ Calendar, List &amp; Holiday Views</h3><ul><li>Calendar view colour-codes presence, absence, and tardiness</li><li>Detailed list view for period-based reporting</li><li>Public holidays overlay automatically on every calendar</li><li>Students, parents, and teachers see the same colour code</li></ul></div>
 </div>
 <p style="margin-top:1.5rem;">Because attendance lives in the same database as fees, scholarships, and discipline, you can apply institutional rules automatically — a minimum-attendance threshold for exam eligibility, a scholarship-retention rule tied to attendance rate, or a disciplinary escalation after N absences. The data is there; the policy is yours.</p>
 </section>

 <section id="fees">
 <h2>Fee Management System — Built for Real School Billing</h2>
 <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;">The <strong>Odoo Education Management System</strong> handles complex, multi-tier fee structures with the same accounting engine powering mid-sized businesses — so your finance team works inside a real ERP, not a simplified school app.</p>
 <p>School fees are never a single number. Tuition, transport, lunch, registration, uniforms, books, and activity fees all stack together — and they're different for every grade. The ERP's Fee Management turns this complexity into clean, grade-wise fee structures that generate invoices automatically and post directly into Odoo Accounting.</p>
 <div class="bento-grid">
 <div class="module-card"><h3>🏗️ Grade-Wise Fee Structures</h3><ul><li>Build one fee structure per grade and session</li><li>Add any combination of fee elements (tuition, transport, etc.)</li><li>Reuse structures across grades with small overrides</li><li>Update fees once; every enrolled student's invoice adjusts</li></ul></div>
 <div class="module-card"><h3>💳 Flexible Payment Terms</h3><ul><li>One-time payment (annual), or recurring (monthly/quarterly)</li><li>Term-wise instalments with auto-generated schedule</li><li>Configurable due dates and overdue reminders</li><li>Online payment straight from the parent portal</li></ul></div>
 <div class="module-card"><h3>📝 Fee Element Library</h3><ul><li>Define fee elements once — tuition, admission, transport, lunch, library</li><li>Mix &amp; match elements into grade structures</li><li>Track revenue by element across the full institution</li><li>Each element maps cleanly into Odoo Accounting journals</li></ul></div>
 <div class="module-card"><h3>📊 Payment Tracking &amp; Receipts</h3><ul><li>Payment status on every invoice: Paid, Partial, Overdue</li><li>Automatic receipts emailed to parents on payment</li><li>Full payment history per student and per parent</li><li>Overdue reminders trigger through Odoo's Marketing Automation</li></ul></div>
 </div>
 <p style="margin-top:1.5rem;">Because Fee Management is native to Odoo Accounting, your finance team gets one reconciled set of books. Every tuition receipt, scholarship deduction, and refund is a proper journal entry — ready for audit, tax season, and year-end reporting without re-entry.</p>
 </section>

 <section id="library">
 <h2>Integrated Library Management — One Card, One System</h2>
 <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;">The <strong>Odoo Education Management System</strong> includes a full library module — issue, return, catalogue, and overdue tracking — linked to each student record and fee account in the same database.</p>
 <p>The integrated library module turns your library into a fully digital operation linked to the main student database. No separate library system, no separate logins, no reconciliation between "who borrowed this book" and "who is this student".</p>
 <div class="card-grid">
 <div class="card"><span class="card-icon">📖</span><h3>Live Library Dashboard</h3><p>See available books, issued books, overdue books, and returns due today at a glance. Drill into any number to see the underlying records.</p></div>
 <div class="card"><span class="card-icon">📷</span><h3>Scanner-Ready Issue &amp; Return</h3><p>Issue or return a book by scanning the library card and the book — or use the manual search for older titles. The transaction stamps against the student profile automatically.</p></div>
 <div class="card"><span class="card-icon">🏷️</span><h3>Rich Book Catalogue</h3><p>Each book has cover images, genre tags, author, ISBN, shelf location, and copy count — making it easy to find, filter, and report on the collection.</p></div>
 <div class="card"><span class="card-icon">📜</span><h3>Full Borrowing History</h3><p>Every issue and return is audited. See which books a student has borrowed across their entire time at the school — and which books a given title has been loaned to historically.</p></div>
 </div>
 <p style="margin-top:1.5rem;">Teachers and librarians use the same interface to issue and return books, while students see their borrowing history in their portal. Overdue books are flagged automatically and integrate with the communication engine for reminders.</p>
 </section>

 <section id="transport">
 <h2>Transport Management — Safe, Tracked, Billed</h2>
 <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;">As a complete <strong>education ERP software</strong>, the <strong>Odoo school management system</strong> manages transport routes, driver assignments, and student pickups — with transport fees added automatically to the student invoice.</p>
 <p>School transport is a safety issue, a logistics issue, and a billing issue all at once. The ERP treats it as one integrated problem — bus routes link to students, students link to pickups, pickups link to trips, and trips link back to transport fees.</p>
